---
id: exhaustive-deps
title: Exhaustive dependencies for query keys
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query keys should contain the serializable values that identify the data returned by your queryFn.\nThis makes sure that queries are cached independently and that queries are refetched automatically when those values change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function call targets are not query key dependencies. For example, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchTodoById(todoId)"},{"type":"text","value":" needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"todoId"},{"type":"text","value":" in the query key, but not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchTodoById"},{"type":"text","value":". Values referenced inside nested callbacks are still dependencies, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"promise.then(() => todoId)"},{"type":"text","value":" also needs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"todoId"},{"type":"text","value":" in the query key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rule-details","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule Details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\" */\n\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todo'],\n  queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId),\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n  detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: ['todo'], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) }),\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const Component = ({ todoId }) => {\n  const todos = useTodos()\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todo', todoId],\n    queryFn: () => todos.getTodo(todoId),\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"const todos = createTodos()\nconst todoQueries = {\n  detail: (id) => ({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => todos.getTodo(id),\n  }),\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"// with { allowlist: { types: [\"Config\"] }}\nclass Config { ... }\nconst Component = ({ todoId, config }: { todoId: string, config: Config }) => {\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todo', todoId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodo(todoId, config.baseUrl),\n  })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowlist.variables"},{"type":"text","value":": An array of variable names that should be ignored when checking dependencies"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowlist.types"},{"type":"text","value":": An array of TypeScript type names that should be ignored when checking dependencies"}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": [\n    \"error\",\n    {\n      \"allowlist\": {\n        \"variables\": [\"api\", \"config\"],\n        \"types\": [\"ApiClient\", \"Config\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-not-to-use-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When Not To Use It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you don't care about the rules of the query keys, then you will not need this rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attributes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Recommended"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🔧 Fixable"}]}],"checked":true}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rule-details","text":"Rule Details","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":3},{"id":"when-not-to-use-it","text":"When Not To Use It","level":2},{"id":"attributes","text":"Attributes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nQuery keys should contain the serializable values that identify the data returned by your queryFn.\nThis makes sure that queries are cached independently and that queries are refetched automatically when those values change.\n\nFunction call targets are not query key dependencies. For example, `fetchTodoById(todoId)` needs `todoId` in the query key, but not `fetchTodoById`. Values referenced inside nested callbacks are still dependencies, so `promise.then(() => todoId)` also needs `todoId` in the query key.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\" */\n\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todo'],\n  queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId),\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n  detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: ['todo'], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) }),\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\nconst Component = ({ todoId }) => {\n  const todos = useTodos()\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todo', todoId],\n    queryFn: () => todos.getTodo(todoId),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nconst todos = createTodos()\nconst todoQueries = {\n  detail: (id) => ({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => todos.getTodo(id),\n  }),\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// with { allowlist: { types: [\"Config\"] }}\nclass Config { ... }\nconst Component = ({ todoId, config }: { todoId: string, config: Config }) => {\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todo', todoId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodo(todoId, config.baseUrl),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Options\n\n- `allowlist.variables`: An array of variable names that should be ignored when checking dependencies\n- `allowlist.types`: An array of TypeScript type names that should be ignored when checking dependencies\n\n```json\n{\n  \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": [\n    \"error\",\n    {\n      \"allowlist\": {\n        \"variables\": [\"api\", \"config\"],\n        \"types\": [\"ApiClient\", \"Config\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you don't care about the rules of the query keys, then you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [x] 🔧 Fixable\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: exhaustive-deps\ntitle: Exhaustive dependencies for query keys\n---\n\nQuery keys should contain the serializable values that identify the data returned by your queryFn.\nThis makes sure that queries are cached independently and that queries are refetched automatically when those values change.\n\nFunction call targets are not query key dependencies. For example, `fetchTodoById(todoId)` needs `todoId` in the query key, but not `fetchTodoById`. Values referenced inside nested callbacks are still dependencies, so `promise.then(() => todoId)` also needs `todoId` in the query key.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\" */\n\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: ['todo'],\n  queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId),\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n  detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: ['todo'], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) }),\n}\n```\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\nconst Component = ({ todoId }) => {\n  const todos = useTodos()\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todo', todoId],\n    queryFn: () => todos.getTodo(todoId),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nconst todos = createTodos()\nconst todoQueries = {\n  detail: (id) => ({\n    queryKey: ['todo', id],\n    queryFn: () => todos.getTodo(id),\n  }),\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\n// with { allowlist: { types: [\"Config\"] }}\nclass Config { ... }\nconst Component = ({ todoId, config }: { todoId: string, config: Config }) => {\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['todo', todoId],\n    queryFn: () => fetchTodo(todoId, config.baseUrl),\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Options\n\n- `allowlist.variables`: An array of variable names that should be ignored when checking dependencies\n- `allowlist.types`: An array of TypeScript type names that should be ignored when checking dependencies\n\n```json\n{\n  \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": [\n    \"error\",\n    {\n      \"allowlist\": {\n        \"variables\": [\"api\", \"config\"],\n        \"types\": [\"ApiClient\", \"Config\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you don't care about the rules of the query keys, then you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [x] 🔧 Fixable\n"}
